{"availability":"available","full":"MirroS-Lab/HarnessEval-W","name":"HarnessEval-W","description":"HarnessEval-W: Agentifying the Evaluation of Visual Worlds","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":307,"forks":10,"created":"2026-08-17T09:50:26Z","updated":"2026-09-07T12:26:31Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mirros-lab.github.io/HarnessEval-W/","topics":["agent","benchmark","evaluation","harness","harness-engineering","kling","minimax-h3","seedance","video-generation","wan","world-model"],"demo":"https://mirros-lab.github.io/HarnessEval-W/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:14.620Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:14.620Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:14.620Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:36.612Z","stars":303,"forks":10},{"at":"2026-10-17T02:58:14.620Z","stars":307,"forks":10}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The era of harnessed benchmarking: evaluation defines the taste of evolution.","A benchmark should deliver more than a scalar score: what makes an evaluation trustworthy is the reasoning that justifies the score. This is especially critical for world models, where judging a rollout requires understanding whether physics, causality, and world state evolve correctly. Humans spot such violations naturally, yet no existing benchmark automates this capability: metrics are computed brute-force, leaving no reasoning chain that can be examined or verified.","HarnessEval is an agentified evaluation pipeline that brings the harness paradigm from the LLM ecosystem to world model benchmarking. Rather than applying a fixed rubric, HarnessEval interprets the context of each evaluation case, decomposes the evaluation question into measurable sub-questions, and spawns specialized sub-agents, each equipped with tailored context and diagnostic tools to reason over its own sub-question. The parent agent then validates the gathered evidence and aggregates it into the final verdict. Every evaluation becomes a transparent evidence tree whose complete reasoning…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MirroS-Lab/HarnessEval-W/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a87be531db4b10c1d6ab3c691bf02ea151818d6254de5a93ffda7b17882fa097","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:36.759Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:36.759Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The era of harnessed benchmarking: evaluation defines the taste of evolution.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MirroS-Lab/HarnessEval-W/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a87be531db4b10c1d6ab3c691bf02ea151818d6254de5a93ffda7b17882fa097","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MirroS-Lab/HarnessEval-W/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:36.760Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-07T12:26:31Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MirroS-Lab/HarnessEval-W/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:36.760Z","hash":"a87be531db4b10c1d6ab3c691bf02ea151818d6254de5a93ffda7b17882fa097","originalBytes":8207,"storedBytes":8207,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:36.612Z","subjects":["Image, audio & video AI"],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Other","subjects":["Image, audio & video AI"],"evidence":[{"subject":"Image, audio & video AI","source":"metadata","match":"video generation"}],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["Science","MCP servers & agents"],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"https://mirros-lab.github.io/HarnessEval-W/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-18T05:16:21.652Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-18T05:16:21.652Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-18T05:16:21.652Z","target":"https://mirros-lab.github.io/HarnessEval-W/","failureCount":0,"consecutiveTemporaryFailures":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-25T05:16:21.652Z"},"previewAttemptAt":"2026